---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site.mjs';
---

<Base
  title="About | The Funding Desk"
  description="The Funding Desk is a plain-English publication and lender helping business owners and property investors understand finance before they apply."
>
  <section class="masthead" style="padding-bottom:1rem;">
    <div class="container">
      <span class="eyebrow">About</span>
      <h1>Why the jargon has to go</h1>
      <p class="sub">{site.masthead} We publish the guides first, then let the products speak for themselves — because the price list shouldn’t be behind a phone call.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top:0.5rem;">
    <div class="container" style="max-width:820px;">
      <div class="section-head">
        <span class="eyebrow">The idea</span>
        <h2>Good decisions need plain language and published prices</h2>
      </div>
      <p style="color:var(--muted);">
        Business owners and property investors are told to “just call us”. We think the opposite order works better:
        learn first, compare second, apply third. Every guide here is written to survive contact with an actual underwriter.
      </p>
      <ul class="tick-list">
        <li>Rates and fee schedules published, not gated behind a form.</li>
        <li>Every acronym in the glossary before it appears in a headline.</li>
        <li>An exit strategy and worked examples in every product guide.</li>
        <li>Applications held by the same underwriter from start to finish.</li>
      </ul>
      <div style="margin-top:1.6rem;">
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="/library/">Browse the library</a> {''}
        <a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/compare/">Open the comparison table</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>